<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/060E">Remark <span data-tag="060E">8.5.6.9</span>.</a> Let $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}' \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a Morita equivalence of simplicial sets. Then pullback along $F$ induces a bijection </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \{  \textnormal{Cocartesian Fibrations $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$} \}  / \textnormal{Equivalence} \ar [d] \\ \{  \textnormal{Cocartesian Fibrations $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}' \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}'$} \}  / \textnormal{Equivalence}. } \]
</div>
<p> Moreover, if $\kappa $ is an uncountable cardinal, then a cocartesian fibration $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is essentially $\kappa $-small if and only if its pullback $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}' \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}'$ is essentially $\kappa $-small. This follows from the classification of Theorem <a data-tag="028K" href="/tag/028K">5.6.0.2</a>, since the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{&lt; \kappa }$ is idempotent-complete (Example <a data-tag="040Q" href="/tag/040Q">8.5.4.22</a>). </p>
</article>
